WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.974
Our first extension goes back to the fat tails.

00:00:03.424 --> 00:00:05.962
The standard GARCH assumes normal shocks.

00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:08.757
What if we let the shocks have heavier tails?

00:00:09.207 --> 00:00:13.071
The Student t distribution has a degrees of freedom parameter, nu.

00:00:13.521 --> 00:00:16.160
Small nu puts much more weight in the tails.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.366
As nu grows, the curve becomes the normal.

00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:24.914
The generalized error distribution, or GED, has a shape parameter instead.

00:00:25.364 --> 00:00:27.270
Shape two is exactly normal.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.476
Below two the peak sharpens and the tails get heavier.

00:00:30.926 --> 00:00:33.125
Shape one is the Laplace distribution.

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:41.572
When we let the data choose, the fitted nu values have a median of about 5, and the GED shapes a median of about 1.3.

00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:44.998
The data clearly prefer heavier tails than the normal.
